<wpf:ResourceDictionary xml:space="preserve"
                        xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
                        xmlns:s="clr-namespace:System;assembly=mscorlib"
                        xmlns:ss="urn:shemas-jetbrains-com:settings-storage-xaml"
                        xmlns:wpf="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation">

  <!--
    Project-scoped ReSharper severities for the Qodana Community for .NET scan. See
    TotallyHotArcRouter.Qodana.slnx.DotSettings for why these decisions live in .DotSettings files
    rather than in qodana.yaml.

    "This return type can be made non-nullable."

    Both sites are StaticAnalyzerTests' Fixed and Throws doubles, implementing IStaticAnalyzer.Analyze
    - which returns StaticAnalysisFinding? because an analyzer with nothing to report returns null.
    That one stub always returns a finding, and another always throws before returning at all, says
    nothing about the contract they stand in for. Narrowing them would make the doubles diverge from
    the interface they exist to impersonate, which is the one thing a double must not do.

    The same decision is recorded for the six sites in TotallyHotArcRouter.Tests. This file exists
    because these two live in a different project, and .DotSettings severities do not inherit across
    projects.
  -->
  <s:String x:Key="/Default/CodeInspection/Highlighting/InspectionSeverities/=ReturnTypeCanBeNotNullable/@EntryIndexedValue">DO_NOT_SHOW</s:String>

</wpf:ResourceDictionary>
